/* =====================================================================================
 *  My-Dro  -  ESP32 Quadcopter Flight Controller  (X configuration)
 * =====================================================================================
 *
 *  WHAT THIS IS
 *  ------------
 *  A single-file, clean, heavily-commented flight controller for an ESP32-based drone.
 *  It reads a FlySky/iBUS receiver, reads an LSM9DS1 IMU, fuses the sensors into a
 *  stable roll/pitch/yaw estimate, runs a PID stabiliser, and drives 4 ESCs at
 *  50 Hz / 11-bit resolution (as requested). A GPS module is read non-blocking and its
 *  data is made available for telemetry and (optional) navigation.
 *
 *  This sketch was written from scratch to be READABLE, DEBUGGABLE and SAFE. It replaces
 *  the older multi-tab "Drone" project which had several real bugs:
 *     - IMU calibration values were assigned to LOCAL shadow variables, so the global
 *       gyro-rate values used by the PID were never actually updated.
 *     - The receiver channels were mapped inconsistently (roll/pitch/throttle swapped).
 *     - The GPS was read with a blocking delay(1000) inside the flight loop, which
 *       throttled the whole control loop down to ~1 Hz (a drone cannot fly like that).
 *     - The heading-error wrap used `while (err < 180)` instead of `< -180` (infinite loop risk).
 *     - There was no real arming sequence or receiver-loss failsafe.
 *
 *  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *  HOW THE CODE IS ORGANISED (read top to bottom)
 *    1. CONFIG            - pins, tuning gains, limits. THIS is the part you edit.
 *    2. GLOBAL STATE      - shared runtime variables.
 *    3. SENSORS           - IMU init + attitude estimation (complementary filter).
 *    4. RECEIVER (iBUS)   - stick + switch decoding, with failsafe.
 *    5. PID               - roll/pitch angle hold + yaw rate control.
 *    6. MOTOR MIXER       - converts PID output to 4 ESC signals (50 Hz / 11-bit).
 *    7. GPS               - non-blocking parsing + telemetry.
 *    8. SAFETY / ARMING   - arm/disarm state machine, kill switch, tilt cutoff, failsafe.
 *    9. DEBUG             - toggleable serial printing so you can inspect everything.
 *   10. setup() / loop()  - wiring everything together at a fixed control rate.
 *
 *  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *  REQUIRED LIBRARIES (install via Arduino Library Manager)
 *    - Adafruit LSM9DS1     (by Adafruit)      + Adafruit Unified Sensor
 *    - IBusBM               (by Bmellink)
 *    - TinyGPSPlus          (by Mikal Hart)
 *  Board: "ESP32 Dev Module" using the ESP32 Arduino core v3.x (the ledcAttach()
 *         API used below is the v3.x form). If you are on core v2.x, see the note in
 *         motorsSetup().
 *
 *  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *  !!! SAFETY FIRST - READ BEFORE POWERING MOTORS !!!
 *    - ALWAYS bench-test with PROPELLERS REMOVED first.
 *    - Set your transmitter's FAILSAFE so that on signal loss the THROTTLE channel
 *      drops BELOW its normal minimum (this code detects that and cuts the motors).
 *    - Verify the motor spin directions and the mixer signs (MIX_* below) before flight.
 *    - Keep the ARM switch within easy reach; flipping it to disarm cuts all motors.
 * ===================================================================================== */

